Subject: [PATCH] runtime: reclaim all completed idle pools before command-buffer growth

Share one warm-handle budget across idle pools and reclaim it on encoding threads
before another allocation. A completed pool need not be reused itself to release
its excess command streams. Active and pending pools remain untouched.
Add allocation and idle-reclamation counters to distinguish retained from live work.

