 ## Fast defaults
 
 Completed command pools retain at most 64 warm command buffer handles per pool across both
-levels. Reuse rotates through the oldest idle pool; excess completed handles are freed and
-the driver's recycled cache trimmed on the encoding thread. The pool itself stays alive.
+levels. Before an encoding allocation grows a pool, all idle pools share one 64-handle budget;
+excess completed handles are freed and the driver's recycled cache trimmed on that encoding
+thread. Reuse rotates through the oldest idle pool. The pools themselves stay alive.
 This bounds command-stream storage retained after a heavy frame without changing recorded
 commands or reclaiming anything pending on the GPU.
 
